{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01590",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.23,
      "end_seconds": 7.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.77,
      "text": "Hi, doctor, I came as soon as they called me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.96,
      "end_seconds": 13.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. Tell me why you came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 15.24,
      "end_seconds": 25.52,
      "duration_seconds": 10.28,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I hope it's alright if I stay in for this. We came because of being drowsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.77,
      "end_seconds": 30.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "So, what's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.18,
      "end_seconds": 35.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "I've had it since last Tuesday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.39,
      "end_seconds": 40.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "How troublesome is it day to day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.67,
      "end_seconds": 47.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "Ah, pretty mild, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.98,
      "end_seconds": 50.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.86,
      "end_seconds": 58.73,
      "duration_seconds": 6.87,
      "text": "It usually comes with a high fever. The high fever? That's been since Monday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.74,
      "end_seconds": 64.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "How often do you get it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.22,
      "end_seconds": 69.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "It sort of comes and goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.78,
      "end_seconds": 86.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Nothing like diarrhoea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.86,
      "end_seconds": 89.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "I haven't noticed any diarrhoea."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.45,
      "end_seconds": 94.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "A few quick ones: stiff neck or cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.51,
      "end_seconds": 98.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Oh, no, none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.71,
      "end_seconds": 102.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Any trouble with the waterworks?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.5,
      "end_seconds": 106.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "No, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.96,
      "end_seconds": 113.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.98,
      "end_seconds": 124.65,
      "duration_seconds": 9.67,
      "text": "Years back I got feeling very drowsy from tramadol, so I stay away from it now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.03,
      "end_seconds": 135.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.06,
      "end_seconds": 159.36,
      "duration_seconds": 23.3,
      "text": "I smoke roughly a pack every two days. I'll have a glass of wine with dinner. I retired from the post office two years ago. My husband and I live above the shop. Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.75,
      "end_seconds": 163.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.55,
      "end_seconds": 172.62,
      "duration_seconds": 7.07,
      "text": "I have heart failure. I have thin bones, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.43,
      "end_seconds": 175.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "Is there anything more?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.64,
      "end_seconds": 183.57,
      "duration_seconds": 6.93,
      "text": "Alright, heart failure, that matches what I have here. Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 184.71,
      "end_seconds": 200.14,
      "duration_seconds": 15.43,
      "text": "She is on spironolactone, 25 milligrams, once a day, I give it to her. She is on alendronate, 70 milligrams, once a week, I give it to her."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.29,
      "end_seconds": 204.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Let me take your readings now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.9,
      "end_seconds": 213.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.71,
      "end_seconds": 234.29,
      "duration_seconds": 6.58,
      "text": "Okay: temp 38.7 degrees, pulse is 89 beats a minute, pressure 112 over 69."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.15,
      "end_seconds": 239.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Is that alright, you know, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.81,
      "end_seconds": 245.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "I'll come back to the numbers."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.48,
      "end_seconds": 250.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Now I'm going to do a short physical check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.39,
      "end_seconds": 254.09,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.45,
      "end_seconds": 257.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.3,
      "end_seconds": 278.53,
      "duration_seconds": 8.23,
      "text": "The purple spots do not fade when I press a glass on them, and he is floppy and drowsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.25,
      "end_seconds": 285.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "Please sit back down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.78,
      "end_seconds": 302.02,
      "duration_seconds": 8.24,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: This is probably possible meningococcal sepsis. I can't rule out a viral rash yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 304.02,
      "end_seconds": 307.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "What are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.81,
      "end_seconds": 335.09,
      "duration_seconds": 26.28,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's possible meningococcal sepsis, and we'll know more once the urgent blood tests is back. I'll request urgent blood tests, it'll help with possible sepsis. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. I'll request blood cultures, it'll help with possible sepsis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.96,
      "end_seconds": 354.78,
      "duration_seconds": 18.82,
      "text": "Let's use benzylpenicillin, 600 milligrams, once now, single dose. That's for possible meningococcal sepsis. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well. I am giving an antibiotic injection now and calling an ambulance. We'll catch up straight away. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 359.08,
      "end_seconds": 362.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "No, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 368.12,
      "end_seconds": 369.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}